  "notes": "USAGE:\n{退席|たいせき} is a formal word, often used in meetings, classes, and official proceedings. The opposite is {着席|ちゃくせき} (taking one's seat).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {途中|とちゅう}{退席|たいせき} (leaving partway through)\n- {退席|たいせき}を{求|もと}める (to request someone to leave)\n- {退席|たいせき}を{命|めい}じる (to order someone to leave)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{退出|たいしゅつ} means leaving a room or building entirely, while {退席|たいせき} specifically refers to leaving one's seat or place at a gathering.",
